Task 4: What is the ID of the PCAP file that contains sensative data?
  Nothing special was performed to solve this, I just downloaded the PCAP files from each ID, followed streams using Wireshark, and found the .pcap that contained sensative data.

Task 5: Which application layer protocol in the pcap file can the sensetive data be found in?
  In order to solve this easily, a person would need to know the 7 OSI layers (Physical, Data link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, and Application) and which protocols
  would be utilized in each layer. When analyzing the .pcap file from 0 in wireshark, I noticed TCP, HTTP, and FTP protocols being used. Understanding the OSI layer, I knew the
  protocols I wanted to look into were HTTP and FTP (application layer protocols) since TCP is used at layer 4. I was able to find a password and username being transmitted using
  the insecure FTP protocol.
    Wireshark --> Open --> 0.pcap
      Select packet # 31 --> right click --> Follow --> TCP Stream
        

